item.stdout:
  1	---
  2	name: codex-agent-team-setup
  3	description: Install or update Agent Kit's portable Codex scout, builder, and reviewer profiles and register them in Codex. Use when setting up the project-control agent team on a machine or checking that its Codex configuration is healthy.
  4	---
  5	
  6	# Codex Agent Team Setup
  7	
  8	Install the execution profiles that `project-control` worktree tasks use. The
  9	installer derives every source path from this skill's installed directory, so
 10	the same plugin works from any Agent Kit cache location.
 11	
 12	## Desired Codex Configuration
 13	
 14	Maintain this registry in the user's existing Codex `config.toml`:
 15	
 16	```toml
 17	[agents]
 18	max_concurrent_threads_per_session = 2
 19	
 20	[agents.scout]
 21	description = "Read-only repository scout for bounded discovery, ownership mapping, and evidence gathering before implementation."
 22	config_file = "./agents/scout.toml"
 23	
 24	[agents.builder]
 25	description = "Bounded implementation agent for one accepted change with focused verification."
 26	config_file = "./agents/builder.toml"
 27	
 28	[agents.reviewer]
 29	description = "Read-only independent reviewer for a supplied diff, acceptance criteria, and verification evidence."
 30	config_file = "./agents/reviewer.toml"
 31	```
 32	
 33	Each registered profile owns its model and reasoning settings. Relative
 34	`config_file` paths resolve from the directory that contains `config.toml`.
 35	The scout uses GPT-6 Luna at high effort for bounded research. The builder and
 36	reviewer use GPT-6 Sol at high effort for implementation and independent review.
 37	
 38	## Role Skill Maps
 39	
 40	Each installed profile names its default Agent Kit skills directly in
 41	`developer_instructions`. Skill names are portable because the Engineering
 42	plugin installs them into the host skill catalog; no plugin-cache path is
 43	embedded in the profile.
 44	
 45	- `scout` routes repository, documentation, web, and retained-knowledge
 46	  research to the relevant research skills.
 47	- `builder` routes implementation, debugging, language taste, and changed-code
 48	  validation to the relevant work skills.
 49	- `reviewer` uses `ce-review` for the baseline pass and its deep alias when
 50	  requested. The worktree task lead names separate structural and deletion
 51	  passes. The reviewer runs one pass at a time without spawning agents.
 52	- The worktree task lead owns explicitly requested multi-provider reviews.
 53	
 54	Knowledge-plugin skills are conditional because Engineering and Knowledge can
 55	be installed separately. The Engineering-owned routes are always available
 56	with this setup skill.
 57	
 58	## Workflow
 59	
 60	Resolve this skill's absolute directory as `SKILL_DIR`. Do not assume a fixed
 61	plugin cache path.
 62	
 63	### 1. Inspect before changing anything
 64	
 65	Run:
 66	
 67	```sh
 68	bun "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/install.ts" plan
 69	```
 70	
 71	The command reports creates, managed updates, unchanged files, and conflicts
 72	under `${CODEX_HOME:-~/.codex}/agents`.
 73	
 74	Read `${CODEX_HOME:-~/.codex}/config.toml` if it exists. Plan a narrow edit to
 75	the existing `[agents]` table and its role tables. Preserve comments,
 76	formatting, unrelated tables, and unrelated keys.
 77	
 78	### 2. Configure Codex
 79	
 80	Use `apply_patch` to add or update the desired concurrency key and role tables.
 81	Never replace the whole config file.
 82	
 83	- Reuse an existing `[agents]` table; do not create a duplicate.
 84	- Replace legacy `max_threads = 2` from an earlier Agent Kit setup with
 85	  `max_concurrent_threads_per_session = 2`. Do not overwrite a different
 86	  user-selected concurrency value without confirmation.
 87	- Remove `enabled`, `default_subagent_model`, and
 88	  `default_subagent_reasoning_effort` only when they exactly match the earlier
 89	  Agent Kit defaults. Preserve different user-selected values.
 90	- Add the three role tables exactly as shown. If one already exists with
 91	  different values, report the conflict instead of overwriting it.
 92	- Preserve settings such as `interrupt_message`, comments, formatting,
 93	  unrelated tables, and unknown future keys.
 94	- If the file is absent, create it with only the desired registry.
 95	
 96	### 3. Install profiles
 97	
 98	Run:
 99	
100	```sh
101	bun "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/install.ts" apply
102	```
103	
104	The installer copies `scout.toml`, `builder.toml`, and `reviewer.toml`, then
105	records checksums in `${CODEX_HOME:-~/.codex}/agent-kit/managed-agents.json`.
106	It stops rather than overwriting an unmanaged or locally modified profile.
107	
108	### 4. Verify
109	
110	Run:
111	
112	```sh
113	bun "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/install.ts" status
114	```
115	
116	`status` validates the installed profiles, concurrency limit, and role
117	registry. A non-zero exit means setup is incomplete or a managed file has
118	drifted.
119	
120	Start a new Codex task after setup so the new role registry is loaded.
 40	}
 41	
 42	interface Ledger {
 43	  readonly version: number;
 44	  readonly profiles: Partial<Record<ProfileName, LedgerProfile>>;
 45	}
 46	
 47	interface InstallPaths {
 48	  readonly agentsDir: string;
 49	  readonly configPath: string;
 50	  readonly ledgerPath: string;
 51	  readonly assetsDir: string;
 52	}
 53	
 54	const desiredAgentConfig = {
 55	  max_concurrent_threads_per_session: 2,
 56	  scout: {
 57	    description: "Read-only repository scout for bounded discovery, ownership mapping, and evidence gathering before implementation.",
 58	    config_file: "./agents/scout.toml",
 59	  },
 60	  builder: {
 61	    description: "Bounded implementation agent for one accepted change with focused verification.",
 62	    config_file: "./agents/builder.toml",
 63	  },
 64	  reviewer: {
 65	    description: "Read-only independent reviewer for a supplied diff, acceptance criteria, and verification evidence.",
 66	    config_file: "./agents/reviewer.toml",
 67	  },
 68	} as const;
 69	
 70	function checksum(content: string): string {
 71	  return createHash("sha256").update(content).digest("hex");
 72	}
 73	
 74	function isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {
 75	  return typeof value === "object" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);
 76	}
 77	
 78	function resolvePaths(options: InstallOptions): InstallPaths {
 79	  const codexHome = path.resolve(options.codexHome);
 80	  return {
 81	    agentsDir: path.join(codexHome, "agents"),
 82	    configPath: path.join(codexHome, "config.toml"),
 83	    ledgerPath: path.join(codexHome, "agent-kit", "managed-agents.json"),
 84	    assetsDir: options.assetsDir
 85	      ? path.resolve(options.assetsDir)
 86	      : path.resolve(import.meta.dir, "../assets/agents"),
 87	  };
 88	}
 89	
 90	async function readOptional(filePath: string): Promise<string | null> {
 91	  try {
 92	    return await readFile(filePath, "utf8");
 93	  } catch (error) {
 94	    if (isRecord(error) && error.code === "ENOENT") return null;
 95	    throw error;
 96	  }
 97	}
 98	
 99	async function atomicWrite(filePath: string, content: string): Promise<void> {
100	  await mkdir(path.dirname(filePath), { recursive: true });
101	  const temporaryPath = path.join(path.dirname(filePath), `.${path.basename(filePath)}.${randomUUID()}.tmp`);
102	  try {
103	    await writeFile(temporaryPath, content, { encoding: "utf8", mode: 0o600 });
104	    await rename(temporaryPath, filePath);
105	  } catch (error) {
106	    await rm(temporaryPath, { force: true });
107	    throw error;
108	  }
109	}
110	
111	async function loadTemplates(assetsDir: string): Promise<readonly Template[]> {
112	  return await Promise.all(
113	    PROFILE_NAMES.map(async (name) => {
114	      const assetPath = path.join(assetsDir, `${name}.toml`);
115	      const content = await readFile(assetPath, "utf8");
116	      const parsed: unknown = Bun.TOML.parse(content);
117	      if (!isRecord(parsed)) throw new Error(`${assetPath} must contain a TOML table.`);
118	      for (const key of ["model", "model_reasoning_effort", "developer_instructions", "sandbox_mode"] as const) {
119	        if (typeof parsed[key] !== "string" || parsed[key].length === 0) {
120	          throw new Error(`${assetPath} must define a non-empty ${key}.`);
121	        }
122	      }
123	      return { name, content, checksum: checksum(content) };
124	    }),
125	  );
126	}
127	
128	async function readLedger(ledgerPath: string): Promise<Ledger> {
129	  const content = await readOptional(ledgerPath);
130	  if (content === null) return { version: LEDGER_VERSION, profiles: {} };
131	
132	  const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(content);
133	  if (!isRecord(parsed) || parsed.version !== LEDGER_VERSION || !isRecord(parsed.profiles)) {
134	    throw new Error(`Invalid Agent Kit profile ledger: ${ledgerPath}`);
135	  }

